#!/usr/bin/env srr-uvrun
"""SRR external ingest strategy: a Telegram channel (incl. PRIVATE) -> SRR items.

Reads a Telegram channel and turns each message — or each album — into an SRR
article, self-hosting its photos and videos into the SRR store. Two modes:

  * ACCOUNT (MTProto) mode — the DEFAULT: private (and public) channels via
    your own user account (the Telethon library). Needs the one-time login
    below.
  * WEB (no-account) mode — `srr-telegram --no-auth`: public channels via the
    public web preview (https://t.me/s/<username>). Needs no credentials at
    all. Media is linked, not downloaded, unless --selfhost is also given.

Dependencies are declared once for the whole toolbox in the repo-root
pyproject.toml and managed by `uv`: the shebang runs the script via the
`srr-uvrun` wrapper (bin/srr-uvrun), which locates the repo from its own
path and execs `uv run --project <repo> --script`, syncing the project's
.venv on first run (see uv.lock for the pinned versions). Both `uv` and the
repo's bin/ must be on PATH — including the PATH of whatever runs the SRR
fetch loop.

Why a user account and not a bot: a bot can only see channels it has been added
to (as admin), can't read history before it joined, and the Bot API caps media
downloads at ~20 MB. A user session reads any channel/group YOU are a member of
and downloads media of any size.

ONE-TIME SETUP (skip if you only use --no-auth)
-----------------------------------------------
1. Install uv (https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) if it isn't already.
2. Get an API id + hash from https://my.telegram.org  ->  "API development tools".
3. Mint a login session (interactive: phone number, login code, optional 2FA):

     export SRR_TG_API_ID=1234567
     export SRR_TG_API_HASH=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
     srr-telegram login            # prints a StringSession + the env lines to keep

   Save the three SRR_TG_* values where the SRR fetch loop can see them (e.g. the
   srr-fetch service environment, or an env file it sources). The session
   string is a credential — treat it like a password.

SUBSCRIBE A CHANNEL
-------------------
The channel's SRR `url` is any of: a private link `https://t.me/c/<id>` (open the
channel in Telegram Web/Desktop to read the id off the URL), a public
`https://t.me/<username>` / `@username`, an invite link `https://t.me/+<hash>`
(you must already be a member), or a bare numeric id (`-100…`).

     srr dev chan add -t "My private channel" \
       -u "https://t.me/c/1234567890" \
       -i "srr-telegram"

Preview without deploying (media is NOT downloaded in preview — placeholders shown):
     SRR_TG_API_ID=… SRR_TG_API_HASH=… SRR_TG_SESSION=… \
       srr dev preview "https://t.me/c/1234567890" -i "srr-telegram" -a 127.0.0.1:8098

WEB (NO-ACCOUNT) MODE — `--no-auth`
-----------------------------------
Public channels need no account: with --no-auth, srr-telegram scrapes the
channel's public web preview instead. No credentials, no setup:

     srr dev chan add -t "Durov" -u "https://t.me/s/durov" -i "srr-telegram --no-auth"

Any public-username URL form works (https://t.me/s/<name>, https://t.me/<name>,
@<name>). Private forms (t.me/c/<id>, invite links, numeric ids) have no public
preview — subscribe those through the default account mode. `--auth` is
accepted as an explicit synonym for the default.

Media is NOT downloaded by default: each photo/video is replaced by an "open in
Telegram" link, keeping the store text-only for that feed. (Hotlinking is not
an option — the preview CDN's URLs are token-signed and expire.) Add --selfhost
to download media into the SRR store instead, like the account mode does:

     srr dev chan add -t "Durov" -u "https://t.me/s/durov" -i "srr-telegram --no-auth --selfhost"

Trade-offs vs account mode: public channels with previews enabled only; with
--selfhost, videos above the preview size limit have no downloadable URL — an
"open in Telegram" link is emitted instead; voice notes, stickers and documents
are skipped; items carry a different dedup guid than account mode (the preview
page hides the numeric channel id), so switching an existing feed between modes
re-imports its backlog once.

MANUAL RUNS (parameters instead of stdin)
-----------------------------------------
Normally srr drives this script by writing a JSON request to stdin. To test a
channel by hand, pass the URL as an argument instead — the request is built
from parameters and the result is pretty-printed:

     srr-telegram --no-auth https://t.me/s/durov
     srr-telegram --no-auth --selfhost https://t.me/s/durov --asset-dir /tmp/store
     srr-telegram https://t.me/c/1234567890 --etag 517

  <url>                     the channel (same forms as the SRR `url` above)
  --etag <cursor>           resume after this message id (absent = first run,
                            so SRR_TG_BACKFILL recent messages are ingested)
  --asset-dir <dir>         store dir to self-host media into (what srr sends
                            as asset_dir; absent = placeholders instead)
  --max-asset-size <bytes>  per-file media cap (absent/0 = no cap)

ENVIRONMENT
-----------
  SRR_TG_API_ID        (required) numeric API id from my.telegram.org
  SRR_TG_API_HASH      (required) API hash from my.telegram.org
  SRR_TG_SESSION       StringSession string from `srr-telegram login`
  SRR_TG_SESSION_FILE  alternative: path to a file holding that string
  SRR_TG_BACKFILL      first-run: how many recent messages to ingest (default 20)
  SRR_TG_MAX_BATCH     max messages (albums count as members) per fetch (default 200)
  SRR_TG_INCLUDE_DOCS  "true" to also self-host non-image/video documents as links

The media size cap is NOT configured here: srr sends its --max-asset-size as the
per-request max_asset_size, and media over that is skipped with a "[… skipped: too
large]" note in place of it. Keeping one cap (srr's) avoids two drifting apart.

This is protocol boilerplate around Telethon; the SRR external-ingest contract is
documented in ~/ws/srr/backend/README.md (Ingest Strategies).
"""
import asyncio
import html as htmllib
import json
import os
import re
import sys
import urllib.error
import urllib.request

try:
    from telethon import TelegramClient
    from telethon.errors import FloodWaitError
    from telethon.sessions import StringSession
    from telethon.tl import functions, types
except ModuleNotFoundError:
    sys.exit("srr-telegram: Telethon not available — run this script via `uv run` "
             "(its shebang does this) so the repo pyproject.toml dependencies "
             "are installed; do not invoke it with a bare `python3`.")

try:
    import bs4
    from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
except ModuleNotFoundError:
    bs4 = BeautifulSoup = None   # only web (no-account) mode needs it

VERSION = "1.5"


# --- config -----------------------------------------------------------------

def env_int(name, default):
    v = (os.environ.get(name) or "").strip()
    return int(v) if v else default


def env_bool(name):
    return (os.environ.get(name) or "").strip().lower() in ("1", "true", "yes", "on")


BACKFILL = env_int("SRR_TG_BACKFILL", 20)
MAX_BATCH = env_int("SRR_TG_MAX_BATCH", 200)
INCLUDE_DOCS = env_bool("SRR_TG_INCLUDE_DOCS")
AUTH_MODE = True   # cleared by --no-auth in main(); default is the account (MTProto) mode
SELFHOST = False   # set by --selfhost in main(); web mode downloads media only when set


def fnv1a32(s: str) -> int:
    h = 0x811C9DC5
    for b in s.encode("utf-8"):
        h = ((h ^ b) * 0x01000193) & 0xFFFFFFFF
    return h


def log(*a):
    print("srr-telegram:", *a, file=sys.stderr)


def credentials():
    api_id = (os.environ.get("SRR_TG_API_ID") or "").strip()
    api_hash = (os.environ.get("SRR_TG_API_HASH") or "").strip()
    if not api_id or not api_hash:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: SRR_TG_API_ID and SRR_TG_API_HASH must be set "
                 "(get them from https://my.telegram.org)")
    return int(api_id), api_hash


def load_session():
    s = (os.environ.get("SRR_TG_SESSION") or "").strip()
    if s:
        return s
    path = (os.environ.get("SRR_TG_SESSION_FILE") or "").strip()
    if path and os.path.exists(path):
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            return fh.read().strip()
    sys.exit("srr-telegram: no session — set SRR_TG_SESSION (or SRR_TG_SESSION_FILE) "
             "from the output of `srr-telegram login`")


# --- entity resolution ------------------------------------------------------

def short_channel_id(marked: int) -> int:
    """Telethon PeerChannel wants the bare channel id, not the -100… peer id."""
    s = str(marked)
    if s.startswith("-100"):
        return int(s[4:])
    return abs(marked)


async def channel_by_id(client, short_id):
    peer = types.PeerChannel(short_id)
    try:
        return await client.get_entity(peer)
    except (ValueError, TypeError):
        # access_hash not cached yet — refresh the dialog list once (this caches
        # every channel we're a member of) and retry.
        await client.get_dialogs()
        return await client.get_entity(peer)


async def channel_by_invite(client, invite_hash):
    res = await client(functions.messages.CheckChatInviteRequest(invite_hash))
    chat = getattr(res, "chat", None)
    if chat is None:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: not a member of that invite link — join the "
                 "channel in Telegram first, then re-fetch")
    return chat


async def resolve_entity(client, url):
    u = (url or "").strip()
    m = re.match(r"^(?:https?://)?(?:t|telegram)\.me/(.+)$", u, re.I)
    if m:
        path = m.group(1)
        if path.startswith("c/"):
            return await channel_by_id(client, int(path.split("/")[1]))
        if path.startswith("s/"):
            path = path[2:]
        if path.startswith("+"):
            return await channel_by_invite(client, path[1:].split("/")[0])
        if path.startswith("joinchat/"):
            return await channel_by_invite(client, path.split("/", 1)[1].split("/")[0])
        username = path.split("/")[0].split("?")[0]
        return await client.get_entity(username)
    if u.startswith("@"):
        return await client.get_entity(u)
    if re.match(r"^-?\d+$", u):
        n = int(u)
        if str(n).startswith("-100"):
            return await channel_by_id(client, short_channel_id(n))
        return await client.get_entity(n)
    return await client.get_entity(u)


# --- content building -------------------------------------------------------

URL_RE = re.compile(r'(https?://[^\s<>"]+)')


PARA_SPLIT_RE = re.compile(r"\n[ \t]*\n+")


def linkify_escape(text):
    """HTML-escape text and turn bare URLs into <a> links. Newlines preserved."""
    out, pos = [], 0
    for m in URL_RE.finditer(text):
        out.append(htmllib.escape(text[pos:m.start()]))
        link = m.group(1)
        out.append('<a href="%s">%s</a>' % (htmllib.escape(link, quote=True),
                                             htmllib.escape(link)))
        pos = m.end()
    out.append(htmllib.escape(text[pos:]))
    return "".join(out)


def text_to_html(text):
    # Telegram separates paragraphs with a blank line (\n\n) and uses a lone \n
    # as a soft line break. Map each paragraph to its own <p> and only soft
    # breaks to a single <br>, so blank lines never become duplicated <br><br>.
    parts = []
    for para in PARA_SPLIT_RE.split((text or "").strip()):
        para = para.strip()
        if not para:
            continue
        parts.append("<p>%s</p>" % linkify_escape(para).replace("\n", "<br>"))
    return "".join(parts)


def classify_media(msg):
    """Return (kind, ext, size) for a downloadable photo/video/doc, else None."""
    if msg.sticker or msg.voice or msg.audio:
        return None
    f = msg.file
    if f is None:
        return None
    ext = f.ext or ""
    mime = (f.mime_type or "")
    if isinstance(msg.media, types.MessageMediaPhoto) or mime.startswith("image/"):
        return ("image", ext or ".jpg", f.size)
    if mime.startswith("video/") or msg.video or msg.video_note or msg.gif:
        return ("video", ext or ".mp4", f.size)
    if INCLUDE_DOCS:
        return ("file", ext or ".bin", f.size)
    return None


class PartialDownload(Exception):
    """A media download ended with fewer bytes than Telegram advertised."""


def unlink_quiet(path):
    try:
        os.unlink(path)
    except OSError:
        pass


def cache_complete(dest, size):
    """A cached file counts only when its size matches Telegram's advertised
    size (fall back to non-empty when the size is unknown) — a leftover from an
    interrupted run must be re-downloaded, never reused."""
    if not os.path.exists(dest):
        return False
    have = os.path.getsize(dest)
    return have == size if size else have > 0


async def media_element(client, msg, chan_id, asset_dir, max_media):
    info = classify_media(msg)
    if info is None:
        return None
    kind, ext, size = info
    if not asset_dir:
        # preview / self-hosting off: there is no public URL for private media.
        return "<p><em>[%s]</em></p>" % kind
    if max_media and size and size > max_media:
        log("skip %s msg %d: %d bytes > cap %d" % (kind, msg.id, size, max_media))
        return "<p><em>[%s skipped: too large]</em></p>" % kind

    rel = "tg/%d/%d%s" % (chan_id, msg.id, ext)
    dest = os.path.join(asset_dir, rel)
    if cache_complete(dest, size):
        # Refresh the mtime so srr's post-cycle age-based cache sweep never
        # deletes a file a live feed still consumes (e.g. while a big backlog
        # warms up across failing cycles).
        os.utime(dest, None)
    else:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dest), exist_ok=True)
        # Download to a .part file and rename into place only once complete, so
        # a run killed mid-download (srr cmd-timeout, crash, dropped
        # connection) can never leave a truncated file at dest for a later
        # cycle to reuse and publish (the live chron-437 moov-less mp4 bug).
        part = dest + ".part"
        try:
            got = await client.download_media(msg, file=part)
        except BaseException:
            unlink_quiet(part)
            raise
        if not got:
            unlink_quiet(part)
            return None
        have = os.path.getsize(part)
        if size and have != size:
            unlink_quiet(part)
            raise PartialDownload(
                "%s msg %d: downloaded %d bytes, Telegram advertises %d"
                % (kind, msg.id, have, size))
        os.replace(part, dest)

    marker = "#/" + rel
    if kind == "image":
        return '<p><img src="%s" alt=""></p>' % marker
    if kind == "video":
        return ('<p><video src="%s" controls preload="metadata" playsinline>'
                '</video></p>' % marker)
    name = (msg.file.name or os.path.basename(rel))
    return '<p><a href="%s">%s</a></p>' % (marker, htmllib.escape(name))


def make_title(caption, chan_title, date_iso):
    for line in (caption or "").splitlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if line:
            return (line[:117] + "…") if len(line) > 118 else line
    base = chan_title or "Telegram"
    return "%s · %s" % (base, date_iso[:10])


def make_link(entity, msg_id):
    uname = getattr(entity, "username", None)
    if uname:
        return "https://t.me/%s/%d" % (uname, msg_id)
    return "https://t.me/c/%d/%d" % (entity.id, msg_id)


def group_messages(msgs):
    """Collapse album messages (shared grouped_id) into one logical post."""
    groups, cur = [], None
    for m in msgs:
        gid = m.grouped_id
        if gid and cur is not None and cur["gid"] == gid:
            cur["msgs"].append(m)
        else:
            cur = {"gid": gid, "msgs": [m]}
            groups.append(cur)
    return groups


async def collect_messages(client, entity, cursor):
    """New messages in ascending id order, bounded by MAX_BATCH (plus a little
    slack so an album straddling the boundary stays whole)."""
    msgs = []
    hard = MAX_BATCH + 32
    if cursor > 0:
        async for m in client.iter_messages(entity, min_id=cursor, reverse=True):
            if not isinstance(m, types.MessageService) and (m.message or m.media):
                msgs.append(m)
            if len(msgs) >= hard:
                break
    else:
        async for m in client.iter_messages(entity, limit=BACKFILL):
            if not isinstance(m, types.MessageService) and (m.message or m.media):
                msgs.append(m)
        msgs.reverse()
    return msgs


async def run_ingest(req):
    api_id, api_hash = credentials()
    session = load_session()
    asset_dir = req.get("asset_dir") or ""
    # srr's --max-asset-size cap, sent per request as max_asset_size (bytes); 0 = no cap.
    max_media = int(req.get("max_asset_size") or 0)
    # Our cursor is the highest message id seen, stored as the etag. A
    # non-numeric etag (e.g. a leftover HTTP etag from a prior #rss strategy)
    # is treated as a first run.
    try:
        cursor = int(req.get("etag") or 0)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        cursor = 0

    client = TelegramClient(StringSession(session), api_id, api_hash)
    await client.connect()
    try:
        if not await client.is_user_authorized():
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: session is not authorized — re-run "
                     "`srr-telegram login`")
        entity = await resolve_entity(client, req["url"])
        chan_title = getattr(entity, "title", None) or getattr(entity, "username", "")
        msgs = await collect_messages(client, entity, cursor)

        groups = group_messages(msgs)[:MAX_BATCH]
        items, max_id = [], cursor
        for g in groups:
            gm = g["msgs"]
            first = gm[0]
            caption = next((m.message for m in gm if m.message), "")
            parts = []
            for m in gm:
                el = await media_element(client, m, entity.id, asset_dir, max_media)
                if el:
                    parts.append(el)
                max_id = max(max_id, m.id)
            body = text_to_html(caption)
            content = "".join(parts) + body
            if not content.strip():
                content = "<p><em>(no content)</em></p>"
            date_iso = first.date.isoformat()
            items.append({
                "guid": fnv1a32("%d:%d" % (entity.id, first.id)),
                "title": make_title(caption, chan_title, date_iso),
                "content": content,
                "link": make_link(entity, first.id),
                "published": date_iso,
            })
    finally:
        await client.disconnect()

    if not items:
        # Nothing new: not_modified preserves the stored cursor + dedup state.
        return {"not_modified": True} if cursor > 0 else {"items": []}
    return {"items": items, "etag": str(max_id)}


# --- web (no-account) mode ----------------------------------------------------
#
# Public channels expose their recent messages at https://t.me/s/<username> —
# plain HTML, no auth. ?after=<id> pages forward (our incremental cursor),
# ?before=<id> pages backward (backfill). Albums arrive pre-collapsed into one
# widget (multiple photo wraps under the FIRST member's id). Photo/video CDN
# URLs are token-signed and expire, so media is downloaded at fetch time, never
# hotlinked. Nonexistent/private/no-preview channels return HTTP 200 with
# neither channel info nor message widgets.

WEB_UA = ("Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) "
          "Chrome/126.0 Safari/537.36")
WEB_PAGE_SIZE = 20   # t.me/s serves at most 20 messages per page

USERNAME_URL_RE = re.compile(
    r"^(?:https?://)?(?:t|telegram)\.me/(?:s/)?([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,})/?(?:[?#].*)?$",
    re.I)
BG_URL_RE = re.compile(r"background-image:\s*url\('([^']+)'\)")
# In the widget's rich text, <br><br>-runs separate paragraphs (same role as
# \n\n in the MTProto message text).
BR_PARA_RE = re.compile(r"(?:\s*<br>\s*){2,}")
KEEP_TAGS = {"b", "strong", "i", "em", "u", "s", "del", "code", "pre"}


def web_username(url):
    """The public username a URL names, else None (private/invite/numeric forms)."""
    u = (url or "").strip()
    if u.startswith("@"):
        u = "t.me/" + u[1:]
    m = USERNAME_URL_RE.match(u)
    return m.group(1) if m else None


def web_get(url):
    r = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={"User-Agent": WEB_UA})
    with urllib.request.urlopen(r, timeout=30) as resp:
        return resp.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")


def _in_quoted_block(el):
    """True for nodes inside a reply quote or a link-preview card — that content
    belongs to another message/page, not to this post's body."""
    return el.find_parent(
        class_=re.compile(r"tgme_widget_message_(reply|link_preview)")) is not None


def _abs_href(href):
    if href.startswith("//"):
        return "https:" + href
    if href.startswith("/"):
        return "https://t.me" + href
    return href


def _clean_rich(node, out):
    """Rebuild t.me rich text keeping only allowlisted markup. Emoji <i> wrappers
    (and <tg-emoji>) collapse to the plain emoji character; unknown tags unwrap."""
    for child in node.children:
        if isinstance(child, bs4.Comment):
            continue
        if isinstance(child, bs4.NavigableString):
            out.append(htmllib.escape(str(child)))
            continue
        if not isinstance(child, bs4.Tag):
            continue
        name = child.name.lower()
        if name == "br":
            out.append("<br>")
        elif "emoji" in (child.get("class") or []):
            out.append(htmllib.escape(child.get_text()))
        elif name == "a":
            href = _abs_href((child.get("href") or "").strip())
            inner = []
            _clean_rich(child, inner)
            body = "".join(inner) or htmllib.escape(href)
            if href:
                out.append('<a href="%s">%s</a>'
                           % (htmllib.escape(href, quote=True), body))
            else:
                out.append(body)
        elif name in KEEP_TAGS:
            inner = []
            _clean_rich(child, inner)
            out.append("<%s>%s</%s>" % (name, "".join(inner), name))
        else:
            _clean_rich(child, out)


def widget_text_html(text_el):
    """Rich-text div -> clean <p> paragraphs; same invariant as text_to_html:
    paragraph breaks never surface as <br><br>."""
    if text_el is None:
        return ""
    out = []
    _clean_rich(text_el, out)
    parts = []
    for para in BR_PARA_RE.split("".join(out).strip()):
        para = re.sub(r"^(?:\s*<br>\s*)+|(?:\s*<br>\s*)+$", "", para).strip()
        if para:
            parts.append("<p>%s</p>" % para)
    return "".join(parts)


def widget_caption(text_el):
    """Plain-text caption (for make_title): cleaned HTML minus markup."""
    if text_el is None:
        return ""
    out = []
    _clean_rich(text_el, out)
    txt = "".join(out).replace("<br>", "\n")
    return htmllib.unescape(re.sub(r"<[^>]+>", "", txt))


def parse_channel_page(page_html):
    """-> (channel_title, [widget dict] ascending by id, channel_exists)."""
    soup = BeautifulSoup(page_html, "html.parser")
    title = None
    og = soup.find("meta", attrs={"property": "og:title"})
    if og and og.get("content"):
        title = og["content"].strip()
    widgets = []
    for w in soup.select("div.tgme_widget_message[data-post]"):
        user, _, mid = w["data-post"].rpartition("/")
        if not mid.isdigit():
            continue
        t = w.select_one("time[datetime]")
        text_el = next((el for el in w.select(".tgme_widget_message_text")
                        if not _in_quoted_block(el)), None)
        media = []
        for el in w.select("a.tgme_widget_message_photo_wrap"):
            if _in_quoted_block(el):
                continue
            m = BG_URL_RE.search(el.get("style") or "")
            if m:
                media.append(("image", m.group(1)))
        for el in w.select(".tgme_widget_message_video_player, "
                           ".tgme_widget_message_roundvideo_player"):
            if _in_quoted_block(el):
                continue
            v = el.find("video")
            # src missing = video too large for the public preview
            media.append(("video", v.get("src") if v else None))
        widgets.append({
            "user": user, "id": int(mid),
            "date": t["datetime"] if t and t.get("datetime") else None,
            "text_el": text_el, "media": media,
            "poll": w.select_one(".tgme_widget_message_poll") is not None,
        })
    widgets.sort(key=lambda x: x["id"])
    exists = bool(widgets) or soup.select_one(".tgme_channel_info") is not None
    return title, widgets, exists


def _url_ext(u, default):
    ext = os.path.splitext(u.split("?", 1)[0].split("#", 1)[0])[1].lower()
    return ext if re.fullmatch(r"\.[a-z0-9]{2,4}", ext) else default


def web_download(url, dest, cap):
    """Stream url to dest honoring the byte cap. -> 'ok' | 'toobig' | 'error'."""
    tmp = dest + ".part"
    try:
        r = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={"User-Agent": WEB_UA})
        with urllib.request.urlopen(r, timeout=60) as resp:
            clen = resp.headers.get("Content-Length")
            if cap and clen and int(clen) > cap:
                return "toobig"
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dest), exist_ok=True)
            n = 0
            with open(tmp, "wb") as fh:
                while True:
                    chunk = resp.read(256 * 1024)
                    if not chunk:
                        break
                    n += len(chunk)
                    if cap and n > cap:
                        return "toobig"
                    fh.write(chunk)
        if n == 0:
            return "error"
        os.replace(tmp, dest)
        return "ok"
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        log("download failed: %s (%s)" % (url, e))
        return "error"
    finally:
        if os.path.exists(tmp):
            try:
                os.remove(tmp)
            except OSError:
                pass


def web_media_element(kind, src, rel_base, n, asset_dir, max_media, post_link):
    if kind == "video" and not src:
        return ('<p><em>[video too large for the public preview — '
                '<a href="%s">open in Telegram</a>]</em></p>'
                % htmllib.escape(post_link, quote=True))
    if not SELFHOST:
        # Downloading is opt-in (--selfhost); hotlinking is not a fallback —
        # the preview CDN's URLs are token-signed and expire.
        return ('<p><em>[%s — <a href="%s">open in Telegram</a>]</em></p>'
                % (kind, htmllib.escape(post_link, quote=True)))
    if not asset_dir:
        # preview: no store to download into — placeholders only.
        return "<p><em>[%s]</em></p>" % kind
    rel = rel_base + ("" if n == 0 else "_%d" % n) \
        + _url_ext(src, ".jpg" if kind == "image" else ".mp4")
    dest = os.path.join(asset_dir, rel)
    if not (os.path.exists(dest) and os.path.getsize(dest) > 0):
        st = web_download(src, dest, max_media)
        if st == "toobig":
            log("skip %s %s: > cap %d" % (kind, rel_base, max_media))
            return "<p><em>[%s skipped: too large]</em></p>" % kind
        if st == "error":
            return None
    marker = "#/" + rel
    if kind == "image":
        return '<p><img src="%s" alt=""></p>' % marker
    return ('<p><video src="%s" controls preload="metadata" playsinline>'
            '</video></p>' % marker)


def collect_web_widgets(username, cursor):
    """-> (channel_title, new widgets ascending, channel_exists), bounded by
    MAX_BATCH (plus slack, like the MTProto collector)."""
    hard = MAX_BATCH + 32
    base = "https://t.me/s/%s" % username
    if cursor > 0:
        title, widgets, exists, seen, after = None, [], False, set(), cursor
        while len(widgets) < hard:
            t, page, ok = parse_channel_page(web_get("%s?after=%d" % (base, after)))
            title, exists = title or t, exists or ok
            fresh = [w for w in page if w["id"] > cursor and w["id"] not in seen]
            if not fresh:
                break
            seen.update(w["id"] for w in fresh)
            widgets.extend(fresh)
            after = max(w["id"] for w in fresh)
            if len(page) < WEB_PAGE_SIZE:
                break
        return title, widgets, exists
    title, widgets, exists = parse_channel_page(web_get(base))
    while widgets and len(widgets) < min(BACKFILL, hard):
        _, page, _ = parse_channel_page(
            web_get("%s?before=%d" % (base, widgets[0]["id"])))
        fresh = [w for w in page if w["id"] < widgets[0]["id"]]
        if not fresh:
            break
        widgets = fresh + widgets
    return title, widgets[-BACKFILL:], exists


def run_web_ingest(req):
    if BeautifulSoup is None:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: beautifulsoup4 not available — run this script via "
                 "`uv run` (its shebang does this) so the repo pyproject.toml "
                 "dependencies are installed.")
    url = (req.get("url") or "").strip()
    username = web_username(url)
    if not username:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: web (no-account) mode only reads PUBLIC channels "
                 "by username (https://t.me/s/<name>, https://t.me/<name>, "
                 "@<name>) — %r needs the account mode: drop --no-auth" % url)
    asset_dir = req.get("asset_dir") or ""
    max_media = int(req.get("max_asset_size") or 0)
    try:
        cursor = int(req.get("etag") or 0)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        cursor = 0

    chan_title, widgets, exists = collect_web_widgets(username, cursor)
    if not exists:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: no public preview for @%s — the channel is "
                 "private, nonexistent, or has previews disabled; it needs the "
                 "account mode: drop --no-auth" % username)

    items, max_id = [], cursor
    for w in widgets[:MAX_BATCH]:
        post_user = w["user"] or username
        link = "https://t.me/%s/%d" % (post_user, w["id"])
        parts = []
        for n, (kind, src) in enumerate(w["media"]):
            el = web_media_element(kind, src, "tg/%s/%d" % (post_user.lower(),
                                   w["id"]), n, asset_dir, max_media, link)
            if el:
                parts.append(el)
        if w["poll"]:
            parts.append('<p><em>[poll — <a href="%s">open in Telegram</a>]'
                         '</em></p>' % htmllib.escape(link, quote=True))
        content = "".join(parts) + widget_text_html(w["text_el"])
        if not content.strip():
            content = "<p><em>(no content)</em></p>"
        date_iso = w["date"] or ""
        items.append({
            # Different keyspace than account mode (which hashes the numeric
            # channel id — the preview page doesn't expose it): usernames can't
            # be all-digits, so the two can never collide.
            "guid": fnv1a32("%s:%d" % (post_user.lower(), w["id"])),
            "title": make_title(widget_caption(w["text_el"]), chan_title or username,
                                date_iso),
            "content": content,
            "link": link,
            "published": w["date"],
        })
        max_id = max(max_id, w["id"])

    if not items:
        return {"not_modified": True} if cursor > 0 else {"items": []}
    return {"items": items, "etag": str(max_id)}


CLI_PARAMS = {"--etag": "etag", "--asset-dir": "asset_dir",
              "--max-asset-size": "max_asset_size"}


def request_from_argv(argv):
    """CLI parameters -> the same request dict srr sends as JSON on stdin."""
    req, i = {}, 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a in CLI_PARAMS:
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                sys.exit("srr-telegram: %s needs a value" % a)
            req[CLI_PARAMS[a]] = argv[i + 1]
            i += 2
        elif a.startswith("--"):
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: unknown option %r (see --help)" % a)
        elif "url" in req:
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: more than one channel URL given "
                     "(%r, %r)" % (req["url"], a))
        else:
            # Not restricted to things that look like URLs: bare numeric ids
            # (account mode) start with "-" but are channels, not options.
            req["url"] = a
            i += 1
    if "url" not in req:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: missing channel URL (see --help)")
    if "max_asset_size" in req:
        try:
            req["max_asset_size"] = int(req["max_asset_size"])
        except ValueError:
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: --max-asset-size must be a byte count, "
                     "got %r" % req["max_asset_size"])
    return req


def cmd_ingest(req=None):
    # req is built from CLI parameters (manual run) or, when None, read as the
    # JSON request srr writes to stdin (the SRR external-ingest contract).
    pretty = req is not None
    if req is None:
        try:
            req = json.load(sys.stdin)
        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: could not parse request on stdin: %s" % e)

    if AUTH_MODE:
        try:
            result = asyncio.run(run_ingest(req))
        except FloodWaitError as e:
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: Telegram rate limit, wait %ds before retrying"
                     % e.seconds)
        except PartialDownload as e:
            # Fail the cycle so the cursor stays put and the next fetch retries;
            # publishing an article that references a truncated file is permanent.
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: partial download, failing cycle to retry: %s"
                     % e)
    else:
        try:
            result = run_web_ingest(req)
        except urllib.error.URLError as e:
            sys.exit("srr-telegram: t.me fetch failed: %s" % e)
    if pretty:
        # manual run: readable for a human, not byte-compatible with srr's
        json.dump(result, sys.stdout, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        print()
    else:
        json.dump(result, sys.stdout)


# --- login (interactive) ----------------------------------------------------

def cmd_login(argv):
    api_id = (os.environ.get("SRR_TG_API_ID") or "").strip()
    api_hash = (os.environ.get("SRR_TG_API_HASH") or "").strip()
    if not api_id:
        api_id = input("Telegram API id (my.telegram.org): ").strip()
    if not api_hash:
        api_hash = input("Telegram API hash: ").strip()

    client = TelegramClient(StringSession(), int(api_id), api_hash)
    log("a login code will be sent to your Telegram app…")
    client.start()  # interactive: phone number, login code, optional 2FA password
    me = client.loop.run_until_complete(client.get_me())
    session = client.session.save()
    client.disconnect()

    print("\nLogged in as: %s (id %s)\n" % (
        " ".join(filter(None, [me.first_name, me.last_name])) or me.username, me.id))
    print("Save these where the SRR fetch loop can read them "
          "(keep SRR_TG_SESSION secret):\n")
    print("export SRR_TG_API_ID=%s" % api_id)
    print("export SRR_TG_API_HASH=%s" % api_hash)
    print("export SRR_TG_SESSION='%s'" % session)


def main():
    global AUTH_MODE, SELFHOST
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    if "--auth" in argv and "--no-auth" in argv:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: --auth and --no-auth are mutually exclusive")
    AUTH_MODE = "--no-auth" not in argv
    SELFHOST = "--selfhost" in argv
    if SELFHOST and AUTH_MODE:
        sys.exit("srr-telegram: --selfhost only applies to the web mode — "
                 "combine it with --no-auth (the account mode always self-hosts)")
    # --auth is the default; accepted so recipes can spell the mode out.
    argv = [a for a in argv if a not in ("--auth", "--no-auth", "--selfhost")]
    if argv and argv[0] == "login":
        return cmd_login(argv[1:])
    if argv and argv[0] in ("-h", "--help", "help"):
        print(__doc__)
        return
    if argv and argv[0] in ("version", "--version", "-V"):
        print("srr-telegram", VERSION)
        return
    cmd_ingest(request_from_argv(argv) if argv else None)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
